# The package is sent to image builds as a named build context (`COPY --from=
# cyberwave-contracts . /cyberwave-contracts`), which copies the whole directory.
# Without this, a local `make models` or `python -m build` puts its output in the
# context, and BuildKit keys the COPY layer on content -- so build artifacts that
# change on every local run invalidate the pip resolve below it, and `build/lib`
# ships a stale second copy of the package into the image.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore; keep the two in step.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv-smoke/
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
